# Decision Bank target.
#
# Sourced by publish.sh — quote every value; an unquoted one containing a
# space or a colon breaks the source.
#
# NO CREDENTIALS HERE. The token lives in the environment publish.sh runs
# in, defined wherever you already define it. This file is committed and
# holds nothing secret.
#
# Only what differs between deployments belongs in this file. Layout
# decisions — directory names, filename pattern, push message — are the
# publisher's own and live at the top of publish.sh, visible and editable
# there. A setting nobody varies is one more thing that can be set wrong or
# drift out of step with the code.

# Project path, as GitLab writes it: group/subgroup/repo
# publish.sh refuses to run while this is CHANGE_ME. A publisher that
# guesses a destination fails the same way an absent one does, with no
# symptom.
BANK_PROJECT="CHANGE_ME"

# Branch records are written to. No CI and no merge request in the loop —
# the publisher pushes here directly and the write is done when it returns.
BANK_BRANCH="main"

# GitLab host, no scheme. Leave empty to use whatever host glab is already
# authenticated against, which is usually what you want.
BANK_HOST=""
